        <body>
            <div type="edition" subtype="primary" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="la" resp="#JP" source="#autopsy">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/><persName type="attested"><name><expan><abbr>L</abbr><ex>ucius</ex></expan></name> <g ref="#interpunct">·</g> <name><w part="I">Caiat</w></name><gap reason="lost" extent="unknown" unit="character"/>
                    <lb n="2"/><name><w part="I">Argy</w></name><gap reason="lost" extent="unknown" unit="character"/></persName>
                    <lb n="3"/>vixit <g ref="#interpunct">·</g> an<unclear>n</unclear><supplied reason="lost">os</supplied> <gap reason="lost" extent="unknown" unit="character"/>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus">
                <listApp>
                    <app><note>Text from autopsy</note></app>
                    </listApp>
            </div>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#JP">
                <p>Lucius Caiat[---] Argy[---] lived [--] years.</p>
            </div>
            <div type="commentary">
                <p>The nomen could be Caiatius or Caiatinus (from Latium). The nomen is most likely Argyrus (or a variant thereof), although Argynnus is also attested. It seems likely not much is actually lost, with the nomen centred and 'annos' abbreviated and the age following.</p>
            </div>
